    <!-- What's New dialog.
         NOTE: aapt2 applies its string-escape rules inside CDATA too — a bare
         apostrophe is a build error and \' renders as a plain apostrophe.
         Don't "unescape" the \' below, and never put an XML comment inside the
         CDATA block (it would render as literal text in the dialog). -->
    <string name="whats_new_content">
        <![CDATA[
        <b>Signed Builds &amp; Fixes — 1.2.0</b><br/><br/>
        <b>⚠️ One-time reinstall required</b><br/>
        PwnEyes is now a properly signed release build instead of a debug build.
        That changes the app\'s package identity, so this version installs
        <i>alongside</i> your old copy rather than over it.<br/><br/>
        • Uninstall the previous PwnEyes after installing this one<br/>
        • Your saved connections will need to be re-added<br/>
        • This is a one-time step — from here on, updates install in place<br/><br/>
        <b>Fixes</b><br/>
        • Fixed a crash when opening Edit Connections with saved devices<br/>
        • Fixed the add button being invisible in dark mode<br/><br/>
        <b>Bugs Squashed — 1.1.1</b><br/><br/>
        Cleaned up layout hierarchy, removed dead code, trimmed theme cruft.<br/><br/>
        <b>Re-Write 1.0</b><br/><br/>
        PwnEyes has been rebuilt from the ground up.<br/><br/>
        <b>New Features</b><br/>
        • Multi-tab WebView — monitor multiple Pwnagotchis at once<br/>
        • Custom port per connection<br/>
        • Pull-to-refresh on the web view<br/>
        • Auto-refresh on a configurable schedule<br/>
        • Drag to reorder connections<br/>
        • Open any device in your default browser<br/><br/>
        <b>Improvements</b><br/>
        • Smarter connection error messages<br/>
        • Configurable connection timeout<br/>
        • Cleaner settings screen<br/><br/>
        <b>Under the Hood</b><br/>
        • Full rewrite — Bluetooth removed, IP-based connections only<br/>
        • MVVM architecture with Room persistence
        ]]>
    </string>

